<section class="section-shell section-pad" id="architecture">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">04 / How I think about systems</p><h2>Good systems start<br /><span class="muted-heading">with clear boundaries.</span></h2><p class="section-lede">A request moves through focused layers, each with a clear responsibility.</p></div>
  <div class="architecture-panel"><div class="architecture-label"><span>REQUEST LIFECYCLE</span><span class="architecture-line"></span><span>01 — 04</span></div><div class="architecture-flow"><div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon"><i class="bi bi-phone"></i></span><div><span class="arch-step">01 / INPUT</span><h3>Client</h3><p>Web · Mobile · Service</p></div><i class="bi bi-arrow-down arch-arrow"></i></div><div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon"><i class="bi bi-signpost-split"></i></span><div><span class="arch-step">02 / ROUTING</span><h3>API Gateway</h3><p>Validate · Route · Protect</p></div><i class="bi bi-arrow-down arch-arrow"></i></div><div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon"><i class="bi bi-cpu"></i></span><div><span class="arch-step">03 / PROCESSING</span><h3>Business Logic</h3><p>Rules · Services · Events</p></div><i class="bi bi-arrow-down arch-arrow"></i></div><div class="arch-node arch-data"><span class="arch-icon"><i class="bi bi-hdd-stack"></i></span><div><span class="arch-step">04 / PERSISTENCE</span><h3>Database / Cache / Queue</h3><p>Store · Retrieve · Decouple</p></div></div></div><div class="architecture-foot"><i class="bi bi-shield-check"></i> Separation of concerns makes systems easier to change and maintain.</div></div>
